{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `merge_config`, and both visible tests pass. A falsy override like `0`, `\"\"` or `False` now replaces the base value whenever its key is present in the override.\n\nThe old loop only copied values that were truthy (`if override[k]:`). I replaced it with a plain `out.update(override)` on a copy of the base, so the base dict passed in is still left unchanged. I also removed the outdated `BUG` comment.\n\nAn explicit `None` in the override now replaces the base value too, since the key is present. If you'd rather have `None` mean \"no override\", that would need a separate check. `old_merge_config` just calls `merge_config`, so it gets the fix automatically."}]},"session_id":"0b7208f4-b6ea-43b3-9340-df05fcba7225"}
